# core-vendor.manifest — the pin. Names ONE commit of
# agenticapps-eu/agenticapps-workflow-core and a sha256 per file. Machine-read
# by bin/resolve-core-artifact.sh, by install.sh, and by test_migration_0014 /
# test_migration_0015. Do NOT hand-edit a sha: re-pin by recomputing every
# entry at the new commit.
#
# The files this repo still carries are byte-identical to core and carry NO
# local header — a header would itself break the byte-identity it records.
#
# core_commit is a COMMIT, not a branch: a core checkout is a live
# workspace and may sit mid-change on a feature branch, and origin/main
# can advance BETWEEN two commands. Resolve it ONCE and take every file
# from that one revision — a per-file rev-parse is how the gate and the
# harness ended up from different commits on 2026-07-25.
#
# ONE commit covers EVERY file listed, and every file this repo takes from
# core is listed. Consistency among the entries present is not sufficient: a
# manifest naming three of five files is internally consistent while recording
# nothing about the two it omits.
#
# Advancing core_commit therefore means RE-VERIFYING the files already listed
# at the new revision, not just appending the new ones. 750da2e -> 60cd83f was
# verified this way: core#42 touched neither gate file, so both sha256s were
# unchanged and the single-commit claim stayed true rather than becoming a
# convenient fiction about files nobody re-checked.
#
# ── two categories, deliberately different (ADR-0047, ported from claude) ────
#
# RESOLVED — install.sh publishes these into the shared ~/.agenticapps/bin/
#   through bin/install-gate.sh. They are NOT vendored here any more. Vendoring
#   them is what this change removed: the runtime never read the copies — the
#   project hook resolves ~/.agenticapps/bin first — so they existed only to
#   feed the installer, and they drifted. On 2026-07-31 this repo still carried
#   gate 1.3.1 against core's 2.0.0 and wrapper 1.1.0 against 1.2.0, having
#   missed the release in which reviews stopped being enforced.
#
# VENDORED — still on disk, each for a reason it cannot be resolved:
#   resolve-core-artifact.sh is the bootstrap and cannot resolve itself; the
#   two conformance harnesses are executed from the repo by CI. Pinned anyway,
#   and the tests compare the bytes on disk to the bytes named here.
#
# ── the pin ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ef030d0 is core's main at the merge of core PR #49. It carries gate 2.0.0 and
# wrapper 1.2.0 — both unchanged from the previous pin — plus core spec 1.4.0 /
# §20: a conformance harness that scored nothing is no longer green. A named
# target that is absent, empty or unreadable is reported as
# `UNSCOREABLE <label> — <reason>` and fails, instead of printing
# `SKIP (not found)` / `TOTAL: 0 passed, 0 failed` and exiting 0.
#
# That is the same failure this repo already knew about from the other end. The
# pin before last, 636f106, had this repo scoring a 2.0.0-era gate with a
# 636f106-era harness — a stale harness certifies a stale gate. §20 closes the
# neighbouring hole: a harness that scores NO gate at all now says so.
#
# All five entries below were re-verified at ef030d0. Three are byte-identical
# to 6cd3b9c; the two vendored harnesses changed, their sha256s were recomputed
# from this commit, and the copies on disk were replaced with those bytes.
# Advancing core_commit means re-checking every file already listed, not only
# the ones expected to move.
core_repo=agenticapps-eu/agenticapps-workflow-core
core_commit=ef030d0430e6c0df6dc13ab567baab3f9e006dbe

# RESOLVED at install time — not vendored in this repo.
file=bin/openspec-change-gate.sh sha256=4ad996cb7f95ebc45c35177eaad70781c23f166fb14283dc693a8ecc31476780
file=bin/reviewer-cli.sh sha256=9a26ebcda9f8c7e3839778337c1b56a4a421610735c08b8b5de1bb528397b11a

# VENDORED on disk — pinned so the copies are checkable against a fixed commit.
file=bin/resolve-core-artifact.sh sha256=1274598c07c0853b91c08d9b27da85d46cc754eff57b9c456cb79f293caf11ac
file=tools/change-gate-conformance.sh sha256=9ddfd5d641464920a4240c656384db722b3b7738768b09cc2a0beb2a2c3aeb21
file=tools/reviewer-cli-conformance.sh sha256=f5161c8b7025e889eec0c78c3b0d6091d51e630ee2b5585d6e7c721089855011
